<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-ermentrout-corticothalamic-seizure-spirals-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Huang et al. (2004, 2010) & Pinto & Ermentrout (2001) neocortical spiral wave dynamics & phase singularity topology — MorphoEval overall 92.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2013-ermentrout-corticothalamic-seizure-spirals.py` (92.9/100, up from 56.9/100 in Pass 1; +36.0 overall). The remediated script solves the 2D excitatory-adaptation Wilson-Cowan / Pinto-Ermentrout neural field PDE with 2D FFT Gaussian intracortical axonal footprint K_e * u, complex state-space phase map phi(x,y,t), and automatic 2x2 plaquette topological phase winding number tracker W_{i,j} = (1/2pi) oint nabla phi . dl across all 6 canonical regimes: CCW single spiral singularity (`W = +1`, `f_rot = 10.52 Hz`, `c_wave = 45.13 mm/s`, radial core amplitude profile `r = 0.9960`), CW mirror spiral (`W = -1`), wave-break figure-eight counter-rotating dipole pair (`N_+ = 1, N_- = 1`, total defects `= 2`, net charge `sum W_i = 0`), expanded axonal footprint (`sigma_e = 0.63 mm`, `c_wave = 69.18 mm/s`), planar wave control (`W = 0`), and CNQX/AMPA glutamatergic blockade quiescent control (`w_ee = 0.8`, `A_rms = 0.0045`, `0` defects), paired with automated CV segmentation of `N = 110` cortical barrel columns (`r = 0.9965`) on `rat_neocortical_tangential_sheet_specimen.jpg` and 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_089_corticothalamic_seizure_spirals.lean`. Overall 92.8/100 (faithfulness 92.8, reproducibility 93.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/corticothalamic_seizure_spirals_comparison.png: rendered output of 2013-ermentrout-corticothalamic-seizure-spirals.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 837189 B, 2227×1863 px, artifact_sha256 5fb972407a691858f812d1fa73ce5ccaef68c4e650f1b3ca25af546cc7dce725 (sha256 5fb972407a691858f812d1fa73ce5ccaef68c4e650f1b3ca25af546cc7dce725), spec_fingerprint 8e19f210a705689fed055999b0cf4bc7b4186b66538d2729cc57db348f32af80. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8e19f210a705689fed055999b0cf4bc7b4186b66538d2729cc57db348f32af80; artifact_sha256: 5fb972407a691858f812d1fa73ce5ccaef68c4e650f1b3ca25af546cc7dce725; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/corticothalamic_seizure_spirals/corticothalamic_seizure_spirals_reference.json=3570a9b466035f9e..., datasets/corticothalamic_seizure_spirals/paper_citations.bib=2ea747169ffdca2a..., datasets/corticothalamic_seizure_spirals/rat_neocortical_tangential_sheet_specimen.jpg=c4fdfb27cd39c842..., datasets/corticothalamic_seizure_spirals/scout_manifest.json=e31d28291faa189a...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-corticothalamic-seizure-spirals-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Huang et al. (2004, 2010) J. Neurosci. voltage-sensitive dye recordings in tangential slices of Rattus norvegicus neocortex demonstrating self-sustained 8-15 Hz theta/alpha rotating spiral waves with radial speed 30-80 mm/s and sharp amplitude reduction A(x_core) -> 0 at the topological phase singularity | Pinto & Ermentrout (2001) SIAM J. Appl. Math. 62:206-225 excitatory-adaptation neural field equations tau_u du/dt = -u + F(w_ee K_e * u - g_a a + I_ext), tau_a da/dt = -a + u governing cortical wave propagation speed and wavelength scaling with horizontal axonal footprint sigma_e | Townsend et al. (2015) J. Neurosci. 35:4657-4662 & Huang et al. (2004) Fig. 4 nucleation of counter-rotating figure-eight spiral pairs (W_+ = +1, W_- = -1, sum W_i = 0) from broken planar wave fronts and suppression by CNQX/AMPA glutamatergic blockade; reconstructed_in_script: 2D Wilson-Cowan / Pinto-Ermentrout excitatory-adaptation neural field PDE solver on a 64x64 (6.0 x 6.0 mm) tangential sheet with 2D FFT Gaussian axonal footprint convolution, state-space phase map phi(x,y,t), and automatic 2x2 plaquette winding number tracker across all 6 regimes | Automated DoG CV segmentation of N=110 tangential cortical barrel columns (mean inter-column spacing 266.8 um) and 50-bin radial cytochrome-oxidase optical density profile (r=0.9965) on rat_neocortical_tangential_sheet_specimen.jpg; transfer_boundary: Normalized excitatory population firing activity u(x,t) in [0,1] and slow adaptation recovery a(x,t) mapped onto the 6x6 mm tangential cortical sheet with 1 ms integration steps; does_not_claim: Full 6-layer vertical Hodgkin-Huxley compartmental dendritic conductances or thalamocortical relay bursting channels." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
